-- title:
--   Norm splitting when F₂⊗_F F₁≅ Z× Z'
-- statement:
--   Let $F$, $F_1$, $F_2$, $Z$, $Z'$ be fields with $F_1$ and $F_2$ finite-dimensional $F$-algebras, and suppose $Z$ and $Z'$ each carry $F$-, $F_1$- and $F_2$-algebra structures forming scalar towers $F\to F_1\to Z$, $F\to F_2\to Z$ and likewise over $Z'$, with $Z$ and $Z'$ finite-dimensional over $F_1$. Assume: (i) the $F$-subalgebra of $Z$ generated by the union of the images of $F_1$ and $F_2$ is all of $Z$, and the same for $Z'$; (ii) $\operatorname{finrank}_{F_1} Z + \operatorname{finrank}_{F_1} Z' = \operatorname{finrank}_F F_2$; (iii) there exist $a\in F_2$ and $b\in F_1$ whose images in $Z'$ agree while their images in $Z$ differ. Then for every $g\in F_1$,
--   $$\mathrm{alg}_{F\to F_2}\bigl(N_{F_1/F}(g)\bigr) = N_{Z/F_2}\bigl(\mathrm{alg}_{F_1\to Z}(g)\bigr)\cdot N_{Z'/F_2}\bigl(\mathrm{alg}_{F_1\to Z'}(g)\bigr),$$
--   where each norm is the determinant of multiplication as a module endomorphism over the indicated base.
--
--   This is the two-factor case of the compatibility of norms with base change along $F\to F_2$, the hypotheses being exactly what forces the multiplication maps to identify $F_2\otimes_F F_1$ with $Z\times Z'$. It is used in the function-field bookkeeping for degeneracy maps on modular curves, via [`AlgebraicCurve.Place.sum_ramificationIndex_mul_inertiaDeg_exchange_add`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Place.sum_ramificationIndex_mul_inertiaDeg_exchange_add) and [`ModularCurve.degeneracyPair_pushforwardAlong_correspondence_levelPrime_identities`](thm.html#ModularCurve.degeneracyPair_pushforwardAlong_correspondence_levelPrime_identities).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_algebraMap_norm_eq_norm_mul_norm_of_adjoin_eq_top.lean

import Mathlib

